---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="The small, explicit telemetry boundary used by qyl.at.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="reading-shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy · qyl.at</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Measure the page, not the person.</h1>
      <p class="lede">qyl.at records a bounded same-origin Core Web Vitals event. The optional Ask AI chat is provided by Tluma, a separate service with its own data practices.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-section editorial-section--raised">
    <article class="reading-shell docs-content">
      <h2>What is recorded</h2>
      <p>LCP, INP, and CLS measurements may be sent with the current pathname, navigation type, viewport dimensions, browser language, and the coarse device-memory value when the browser exposes it. These records are used to evaluate the site’s real-world loading and interaction quality.</p>

      <h2>What is excluded</h2>
      <p>The event does not include URL queries, page or form content, request or response bodies, arbitrary HTTP headers, credentials, account identity, or MCP tool arguments. Unknown fields are rejected by the Worker before export.</p>

      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>The browser posts to <code>/_qyl/vitals</code> on this origin. A Cloudflare Worker validates the closed payload and forwards an official OTLP log record to the qyl collector. The collector credential remains server-side. qyl’s normal telemetry retention policy applies; the performance scoreboard uses rolling 28-day aggregates.</p>

      <h2>Ask AI by Tluma</h2>
      <p>Pages load the chat launcher script from <a href="https://tluma.ai/">Tluma</a>. The hosted chat loads when you open Ask AI; background chat preloading is disabled. The assistant uses the public <a href="https://github.com/ANcpLua/qyl">qyl repository</a> as its source.</p>
      <p>When you open the chat, the widget shares the current page URL with Tluma. Tluma processes your messages, responses, and session information, and may store browser identifiers for conversation continuity. This is separate from the Core Web Vitals event described above. Do not paste secrets or sensitive production logs. See <a href="https://tluma.ai/privacy-policy">Tluma’s privacy policy</a> for access and retention details.</p>

      <h2>Source and questions</h2>
      <p>The site and collector are open source. Implementation questions or deletion requests can be raised through the <a href="https://github.com/ANcpLua/qyl.at/issues">qyl.at issue tracker</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
